In article <01bd2feb$6b952b40$55326489@kunecki-pc.calspan.com>, "Anthony J. Kunecki" <kunecki@calspan.com> writes:
:
:I tried adding a CXY08 interface to my MicroVax 3400 and have a problem
:with connecting to it with VMS sysgen. The CXY08 is configured for DHV11
:emulation and were given a non-conflicting csr and interrupt vector within
:my MicroVax. The board is recognized by the MicroVax in the microcode
:before booting. How do I configure VMS to recognize this interface ?, What
:are the proper commands and syntaxes ?

  There are generally no commands necessary to autoconfigure supported
  Q-bus modules under OpenVMS -- OpenVMS will detect and will configure
  all supported devices automatically during system bootstrap.

  It would appear that the CSR was not correctly encoded on the module
  switchpack, or that the other CSRs on other Q-bus modules that needed
  to be altered to the settings dictated by SYSGEN> CONFIGURE -- either
  prevents autoconfiguration.

  Folks do seem to misconfigure the CSR (and interrupt vector settings)
  from time-to-time, and folks do seem to underestimate the side affects
  that arise when or more Q-bus modules are omitted from the specifications
  during a SYSGEN> CONFIGURE pass.  Either can -- and often does -- prevent
  device autoconfiguration.

  If you wish to entirely manually configure the device, you will need to
  use SYSGEN> CONNECT, specifying the CSR and interrupt vector.  (And this
  assumes unique CSR and interrupt vector settings are used.)

  I will assume that there are no empty slots interspersed between the CPU
  and the last Q-bus module on the bus -- that all slots are contiguously
  occupied.  (Failure to have a correctly configured Q-bus generally means
  bus hangs and odd behaviour when the device is activated, but it does not
  interfere with the device autoconfiguration process -- that process is
  based on the device CSR.)

  The only way to ensure the CSR and interrupt vectors are set correctly
  on a set of Q-bus modules is to examine each module switchpack -- one
  can usually infer the CSR setting is correct, but OpenVMS cannot read
  the interrupt vector settings off the modules in any standard way.

  Also visit www.dejanews.com, and look for other discussions that I and
  others have been involved with on Q-bus operations and on the correct
  Q-bus configuration procedures...

