Anthony J. Kunecki wrote:

> I tried adding a CXY08 interface to my MicroVax 3400 and have a problem
> with connecting to it with VMS sysgen. The CXY08 is configured for DHV11
> emulation and were given a non-conflicting csr and interrupt vector within
> my MicroVax. The board is recognized by the MicroVax in the microcode
> before booting. How do I configure VMS to recognize this interface ?, What
> are the proper commands and syntaxes ?
>
> Currently loaded VMS 5.5-2 operating system.


No commands should be needed. VMS automatically will configure this device
at the boot time so you should see devices TXA0...TXA7 if that CXY08 was
your first multiplexor board. You have checked already that the terminal line
are not seen by VMS? ($ show device TX)

Giving the board non-conflicting csr etc may not be exactly the required
thing.
You have to give it non-conflicting approriarite settings. The thing to do is:

$ mc sysgen show /unibus

and

>>> show qbus

Compare these two and also do

$ mc sysgen
SYSGEN> configure

and feed to this all the QBUS devices on the bus and compare the end result
with your actual settings.


_veli






