There is no such function in standard C. It's a UNIX/POSIX function.  My man
page for it says that it may return NULL; it could be that the implementors
simply chose to have it return NULL each time it is called, allowing programs
which use popen to compile but not actually invoke the functionality. Given
that, as you say, the function wasn't supported at all in a previous version
of the system, this wouldn't be surprising.

I think you are lost in search for an OpenVMS programming newsgroup.



