>
>I am also interested in DCL commands and SORT/MERGE specification files
that
>will allow me to manipulate records with a date/time key.


Sorting a list of dates is strait forward enough. Supposing
a file containing a list of dates (something along the lines of):

01-JAN-1998
25-MAR-1945
05-SEP-1999

a specification file to do the trick would run as follows:

(order.srt)

/collating_sequence=(sequence=
    "AN","EB","AR","PR","AY","UN","UL",
    "UG","EP","CT","OV","EC","0"-"9"),
    modification=(" "="0"),
    fold)
/field=(name=year,pos:8,siz:4)\
/field=(name=month,pos:4,siz:3)
/field=(name=day,pos:1,siz:2)
/key=year
/key=month
/key=day

Assuming the above dates are in a file called dates.dat a

    $ sort/spec=order.srt dates.dat sys$output

would list them in sorted order on your terminal.

